[size=3][color=#f2c078][b]Version 0.9.6 - public beta[/b][/color][/size][/center]
Thanks for trying BG3RTX. This is a [b]public beta[/b], tested in a limited set of places and on one card only, an [b]RTX 5090[/b]. Your reports decide what gets fixed first.
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3474/images/26453/26453-1793822874-8567818.png[/img]
[list]
[*]The game must use the [b]Vulkan[/b] renderer and [b]DLSS[/b]. DirectX 11 is not supported; Ray Reconstruction does not run with FSR, XeSS or TAA.
[*][b]NVIDIA RTX only.[/b] Frame generation 2x needs RTX 40 or newer; 3x and 4x need RTX 50.
[*]Start with [b]Low[/b] and raise settings step by step. There are no tested VRAM recommendations yet.
[*]The [b]first start[/b] compiles shaders: expect a slower load and some stutter once.
[*][b]Ctrl+Shift+F9[/b] switches all ray tracing off and on in game, to check whether a problem comes from BG3RTX (change it in the launcher, Hotkeys).
[*][b]New in 0.9.6:[/b] less video memory, a clearer launcher, [b]RTX Hair[/b] (beta, off by default) that now works, a faster start from the second launch, opacity micromaps back in High and Ultra, a water flicker fixed. See the Changelog.
[*]BG3RTX changes nothing in the game folder, the registry or your saves.
[*]Downloads: [b]Files[/b] tab ([i]Setup.zip[/i] installer or [i]Portable.zip[/i]). Source code (GPL-3.0-or-later): [url=https://github.com/NIGos/BG3RTX]github.com/NIGos/BG3RTX[/url].
[/list]
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3474/images/26453/26453-1793823026-850583066.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Crash at start, or frame generation does nothing:[/b] turn off other overlays (Steam, Discord, GOG Galaxy) for one launch.
[*][b]Stalls, missing geometry or crashes after a while:[/b] usually video memory. Lower the preset or resolution and restart.
[*][b]An option changed nothing:[/b] options marked [i]Restart to apply[/i] need a game restart.
[*]Questions go here. Bugs go on the [b]Bugs[/b] tab, one report per problem.
[/list]
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3474/images/26453/26453-1793823079-1370877169.png[/img]
[list=1]
[*]Turn on [b]Detailed logging[/b] (launcher, Help & support), restart the game and reproduce the problem.
[*]In the launcher: [i]Create a report…[/i], [i]Preview files[/i], [i]Save report…[/i], and attach the file. Nothing is uploaded for you.
[*]Add your GPU and VRAM, driver and game version, other graphics mods, and your preset and changed options.
[*]Say where and what happened. A screenshot with Ctrl+Shift+F9 off and on helps a lot.
[/list]
Turn Detailed logging off afterwards. [color=#f2c078]Please do not post a save file unless asked.[/color]
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3474/images/26453/26453-1793823121-1599587881.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Act 2, most of Act 3 and sessions of several hours are not systematically tested yet. Reports are very welcome.
[*]A reflected surface that is hidden or off screen keeps the game's own reflection for now.
[*]The first start after installing can take 15 to 50 s longer while hair shaders are created. Later starts reuse them.
[*]ReShade works, frame generation included; its AO or GI effects duplicate BG3RTX's work. HDR is not tested.
[*]DLSS 5 Neural Rendering is experimental and costs about 6.7 ms per frame on an RTX 5090.
[*]A new game patch can break BG3RTX until it is updated.
[*][b]RTX Hair[/b]: styles not converted yet stay as the game's hair, and a head seen for the first time shows the game's hair for about half a second.
[/list]
[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3474/images/26453/26453-1793822830-820569208.png[/img]
[size=2][color=#beb5a4]Enjoy the light. See you in the Bugs tab.[/color][/size][/center]
